-- title:
--   Graded pieces of an ideal generated by weighted homogeneous polynomials
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field, $G$ an additive abelian group, $w:\sigma\to G$ a weight function and $R=K[x_\sigma]$; for $d\in G$ let $R_d\subseteq R$ be the subspace of polynomials that are weighted homogeneous of weight $d$. Let $E$ be a finite index set and let $F_i\in R$ ($i\in E$) be weighted homogeneous of weight $e_i\in G$. For $d\in G$ consider the $K$-linear map
--   $$\mu_d:\ \prod_{i\in E}R_{d-e_i}\longrightarrow R_d,\qquad (g_i)_{i\in E}\longmapsto\sum_{i\in E}F_i\,g_i .$$
--   Then its image is exactly the weight-$d$ part of the ideal generated by the $F_i$:
--   $$\operatorname{im}\mu_d=(F_i : i\in E)\cap R_d .$$
--
--   Thus the weight-$d$ piece of an ideal with homogeneous generators consists of the combinations of the generators with homogeneous coefficients of complementary weights. This presents $R_d/\bigl((F_i)\cap R_d\bigr)$ as the cokernel of a linear map that depends linearly on the generators, which is what makes rank arguments possible for families of ideals generated by $(1-s)\,Q_i+s\,F_i$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $\mu_d$ is `homogeneousIdealMap w e F hF d`, defined as the sum over $i$ of multiplication by $F_i$ (from `Piece w (d - e i)` to `Piece w d`) composed with the $i$-th projection. The right-hand side is the preimage of `Ideal.span (Set.range F)` under the inclusion of `weightedHomogeneousSubmodule K w d`, as a submodule of that piece.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Algebra/Determinantal/LinearForms.lean#L344-L366

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_SmoothInitialForm
import Definitions.Def_OAI_Algebra_Determinantal_Multigraded
import Definitions.Def_OAI_Algebra_Determinantal_LinearForms

open OAI OAI.PermanentBorder OAI.PermanentBorder.Multigraded
open MvPolynomial
variable {K σ G E : Type*} [Field K] [AddCommGroup G] [Fintype E]
variable (w : σ → G) (e : E → G) (F : E → MvPolynomial σ K)
  (hF : ∀ i, (F i).IsWeightedHomogeneous w (e i))

theorem OAI.PermanentBorder.Multigraded.homogeneousIdealMap_range (d : G) :
    LinearMap.range (homogeneousIdealMap w e F hF d) =
      ((Ideal.span (Set.range F)).restrictScalars K).comap (Piece (K := K) w d).subtype := by sorry
